# What is listed here never enters the build context, and a file that is not in
# the build context cannot end up in an image layer — not through the COPYs the
# Dockerfile writes today, and not through one a later edit widens. That is the
# guarantee, and it is why the exclusions live here rather than in each stage's
# good intentions: a key that cannot enter the build context cannot end up in a
# layer, and a layer that holds a key has published it to every registry the
# image reaches.

# Credentials and local configuration. ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is read in exactly one
# module and arrives only through `docker run -e`; these two lines are the other
# half of that discipline. Nothing in the build needs them, and an image that
# accidentally contains one cannot be un-published.
.env
.env.*

# The local environment. The image builds its own from uv.lock; a macOS .venv
# copied into a Linux image would be the wrong platform, and it would also
# shadow the one uv installs.
.venv/

# Bytecode and tool caches. Machine-written, host-specific, and stale the moment
# they are copied. .hypothesis holds the example database from local property
# runs — the test image regenerates it, and carrying it in would make a build's
# results depend on which examples happened to be on the builder's disk.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.hypothesis/

# mutmut's mutated copy of the source tree, plus its result database. It is a
# whole second copy of src/ with deliberate bugs written into it, and ruff is
# configured to skip it for the same reason nothing should ship it.
mutants/
.mutmut-cache

# Build output and coverage. The image builds the wheel itself from src/.
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Logs
*.log

# History and editor leftovers, not build input. .git/ is also the largest thing
# in the context by a wide margin.
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.claude/
.DS_Store

# Not needed inside any stage.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# README.md is deliberately NOT excluded, unlike the prose in the four
# TypeScript repositories this file follows. pyproject.toml names it in the
# `readme` field, so hatchling reads it when building the project's metadata:
# without it in the context, `uv sync --locked` fails at the point where it
# installs the project. It is an input here, not documentation.
